{"assets":["/statement-assets/02b7b31f34ed5fc09906253d6d441a8d3382231ea438750eb9429910b7b7df57.png","/statement-assets/754662d197e049c968c5a4131ee7b6cfb3c4a4887cf7812f6367ecae12efc64f.png","/statement-assets/6d22e6acb3786980b5f80d653460e4728c861d80e17188ca2aefff3e1a9b9f38.png","/statement-assets/761f41791732de8e2820546430a10d57e821088ffb6385dfc1b0d3611ccd6948.png","/statement-assets/5db74eed4ccd7b22be9f05b6fdae4b78d4944902d82cad764018c894354e5658.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1968","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Cells Arrangement"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an integer $$$n$$$. You choose $$$n$$$ cells $$$(x_1,y_1), (x_2,y_2),\\dots,(x_n,y_n)$$$ in the grid $$$n\\times n$$$ where $$$1\\le x_i\\le n$$$ and $$$1\\le y_i\\le n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$\\mathcal{H}$$$ be the set of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"distinct"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" Manhattan distances between any pair of cells. Your task is to maximize the size of $$$\\mathcal{H}$$$. Examples of sets and their construction are given in the notes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there exists more than one solution, you are allowed to output any."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Manhattan distance between cells $$$(x_1,y_1)$$$ and $$$(x_2,y_2)$$$ equals $$$|x_1-x_2|+|y_1-y_2|$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1\\le t\\le 50$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the following $$$t$$$ lines contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2\\le n\\le 10^3$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output $$$n$$$ points which maximize the size of $$$\\mathcal{H}$$$. It is not necessary to output an empty line at the end of the answer for each test case."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 1\n1 2\n\n2 1\n2 3\n3 1\n\n1 1\n1 3\n4 3\n4 4\n\n1 1\n1 3\n1 4\n2 1\n5 5\n\n1 4\n1 5\n1 6\n5 2\n5 5\n6 1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first testcase we have $$$n=2$$$. One of the possible arrangements is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/02b7b31f34ed5fc09906253d6d441a8d3382231ea438750eb9429910b7b7df57.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The arrangement with cells located in $$$(1,1)$$$ and $$$(1,2)$$$."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" In this case $$$\\mathcal{H}=\\{|1-1|+|1-1|,|1-1|+|2-2|,|1-1|+|1-2|\\}=\\{0,0,1\\}=\\{0,1\\}$$$. Hence, the size of $$$\\mathcal{H}$$$ is $$$2$$$. It can be shown that it is the greatest possible answer."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second testcase we have $$$n=3$$$. The optimal arrangement is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/754662d197e049c968c5a4131ee7b6cfb3c4a4887cf7812f6367ecae12efc64f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The arrangement with cells located in $$$(2,1)$$$, $$$(2,3)$$$ and $$$(3,1)$$$."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\mathcal{H}$$$=$$$\\{|2-2|+|1-1|,|2-2|+|3-3|,|3-3|+|1-1|,|2-2|+|1-3|,|2-3|+|1-1|,|2-3|+|3-1|\\}$$$=$$$\\{0,0,0,2,1,3\\}$$$=$$$\\{0,1,2,3\\}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For $$$n=4$$$ a possible arrangement is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/6d22e6acb3786980b5f80d653460e4728c861d80e17188ca2aefff3e1a9b9f38.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For $$$n=5$$$ a possible arrangement is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/761f41791732de8e2820546430a10d57e821088ffb6385dfc1b0d3611ccd6948.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For $$$n=6$$$ a possible arrangement is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/5db74eed4ccd7b22be9f05b6fdae4b78d4944902d82cad764018c894354e5658.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1968E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1968/problem/E"}